          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em complex oriented cohomology theory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theory"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theory
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} oriented
            on all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology"} cobordism cohomology
          %p
            The collection of all complex oriented cohomology theories turns out to be parameterized over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+formal+group+laws"} moduli stack of formal group laws
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratification"} stratification
            of this stack by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/height+of+a+formal+group"} height of formal group
            leads to the stratification of complex oriented cohomology theory by “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+level"}> chromatic level
            ”, a perspective also known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
          %p
            For more detailed introduction see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Cobordism+and+Complex+Oriented+Cohomology"} Introduction to Cobordism and Complex Oriented Cohomology
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#DefInTermsOfGeneralizedFirstChernClass In terms of generalized first Chern classes
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^\infty \simeq B U(1) \simeq K(\mathbb{Z},2)
            for the infinite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            (an
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i \;\colon\; S^2\cong\mathbb{C}P^1\hookrightarrow\mathbb{C}P^\infty\cong B U(1)
          %p
            for a representative of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathbb{Z} \simeq  \pi_2(B U(1))
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+line+bundle"} universal complex line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+homotopy+types"} pointed homotopy types
            and take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            to be a pointed morphism.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \pi_\bullet[X,E]
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"} reduced cohomology
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            there is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            decomposition (
            %a{:href => "generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology#UnreducedCohomologyIsReducedPlusPointValue"}> this prop.
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^\bullet(X) \simeq \tilde E^\bullet(X) \oplus E^\bullet(\ast)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"} suspension isomorphism
            there is an identification
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mn 2
