                \:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Cobordism+and+Complex+Oriented+Cohomology"} Introduction to Cobordism and Complex Oriented Cohomology
                (2016)
            %li#Pedrotti16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+Pedrotti"}> Riccardo Pedrotti
                \:
                %em Complex oriented cohomology, generalized orientation and Thom isomorphism
                (2016, 2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PedrotticECohomology2018.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
            originates in
          %ul
            %li#Hopkins99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+oriented+cohomology+theories+and+the+language+of+stacks"} Complex oriented cohomology theories and the language of stacks
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HopkinsComplexOrientedCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p and is further developed in
          %ul
            %li#LurieLecture
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252x.html"} web
              %p
                Lecture 4
                %em Complex-oriented cohomology theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture4.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p
                Lecture 6
                %em MU and complex orientations
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture6.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            See also the references at
            = succeed "-." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "equivariant+cohomology#InComplexOrientedGeneralizedCohomologyTheory"} equivariant cohomology – References – Complex oriented cohomology
          %p
            A comparison between complex orientations and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\infty
            ring maps out of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            was given in
          %ul
            %li#Ando92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              %em Operations in complex-oriented cohomology theories related to subgroups of formal groups
              (
              %a{:href => "https://dspace.mit.edu/bitstream/handle/1721.1/13230/26903638-MIT.pdf?sequence=2"}> PhD Thesis
              )
          %p More recent developments include
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsLawson16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tyler+Lawson"} Tyler Lawson
                %em Strictly commutative complex orientation theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1603.00047"}> arXiv:1603.00047
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doron+Grossman-Naples"}> Doron Grossman-Naples
                ,
                %em Complex Orientations are Partial Strictifications of the Unit
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.01663"}> arXiv:2311.01663
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Refinement to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} equivariant complex oriented cohomology theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant formal group laws and complex oriented cohomology theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.hha/1139840255"} euclid:hha/1139840255
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Cole"}> Michael Cole
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"} John Greenlees
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The universality of equivariant complex bordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s002090100315"} doi:10.1007/s002090100315
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesFiniteStageOrientations Finite-dimensional complex orientation and Ravenel’s spectra
            %p
              Discussion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex orientation
              (in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+generalized+cohomology"} Whitehead generalized cohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
              which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pulled back
              from base spaces of
              %em bounded
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              (
              %a{:href => "#Hopkins84"}> Hopkins 1984 §1.2
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Ravenel86"} Ravenel 1986 §6.5.2
              = succeed ")_" do
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber23"} SS23 §3.8
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ravenel%27s+spectrum"} Ravenel's
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectra"} Thom spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(n)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(m)
              (
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel84"}> Ravenel 1984, Sec. 3
              ) which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} co-represent
              these:
            %ul
              %li#Ravenel84
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"}> Douglas Ravenel
                  , §6.5.2 in:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Localization with Respect to Certain Periodic Homology Theories
                  %strong 106
                  2 (1984) 351-414 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2374308"}> doi:10.2307/2374308
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2374308"} jstor:2374308
              %li#Hopkins84
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
                  , §1.2 in:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Stable decompositions of certain loop spaces
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HopkinsStableDecompositions.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li#Ravenel86
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"}> Douglas Ravenel
                  , §6.5 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+cobordism+and+stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} Complex cobordism and stable homotopy groups of spheres
                  %strong 347
                  (2004) [
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/chel-347-h"}> ISBN:978-0-8218-2967-7
                  ]
              %li#DevinatzHopkinsSmith88
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ethan+Devinatz"}> Ethan Devinatz
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Smith"} Jeffrey Smith
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Nilpotence and Stable Homotopy Theory I
                  %strong 128
                  2 (1988) 207-241 [
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1971440"}> jstor:1971440
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"}> Doug Ravenel
                  \:
                  %em
                    The first Adams-Novikov differential for the spectrum
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(m)
                  (2000)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mypapers/first.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RavenelAdamsNovikovForTm.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  Ippei Ichigi, Katsumi Shimomura:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      The Modulo Two Homotopy Groups of the
                      = succeed "-Localization" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi L
                                %mn 2
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_2
                  %strong 10
                  03 43–55 (2008)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://revistas.ufro.cl/ojs/index.php/cubo/article/view/1498"} cubo:1498
              %li
                %p
                  Gabe Angelini-Knoll,
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+D.+Quigley"} J. D. Quigley
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Segal Conjecture for topological Hochschild homology of the Ravenel spectra
                  %strong 4
                  3 (2011) 591-622 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/jtopol/jtr015"}> doi:10.1112/jtopol/jtr015
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.03343"} arXiv:1705.03343
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Beardsley"}> Jonathan Beardsley
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      A Theorem on Multiplicative Cell Attachments with an Application to Ravenel’s
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(n)
                      Spectra
                  %strong 14
                  (2019) 611–624 [
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40062-018-0222-6"}> doi:10.1007/s40062-018-0222-6
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.03042"} arXiv:1708.03042
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Beardsley"}> Jonathan Beardsley
                  \:
                  %em
                    Topological Hochschild homology of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(n)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.09486"} arXiv:1708.09486
              %li
                %p
                  Xiangjun Wang, Zihong Yuan:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      The homotopy groups of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn 2
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi m
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mi m
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
